  "notes": "うなる is an onomatopoeic verb meaning to groan, moan, or growl—making a low, prolonged sound.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nUSAGE BY SUBJECT:\n- Humans: groaning in pain, moaning in thought\n- Animals: growling (dogs, bears)\n- Things: roaring, rumbling (engines, wind)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧うなる: to groan in pain\n- ⟦{犬|いぬ}→犬：00632_inu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧うなる: the dog growls\n- ⟦エンジン→エンジン：03835_enjin⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧うなる: the engine roars\n- ⟦{風|かぜ}→風：00641_kaze⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧うなる: the wind howls\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\nうなるほど + noun: to have an abundance of something (lit. to the point of groaning)\n- うなるほど⟦{金|かね}→金：02618_kane⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦ある→ある：00006_aru⟧: to have money to burn",
